--- version
lube 0.1.0
[exit 0]
--- short version
lube 0.1.0
[exit 0]
--- help
Lube 0.1.0 - a small, smooth scripting language

usage:
  lube                  start the interactive REPL
  lube FILE [ARGS...]   run a Lube script (ARGS are available as `args`)
  lube -e CODE          run CODE and print the value of the last expression
  lube -                read a script from standard input
  lube --check FILE     report syntax errors without running anything (FILE may be -)
  lube --debug FILE [ARGS...]
                        run FILE in the debugger (h at its prompt lists the commands)
  lube --hot FILE [ARGS...]
                        run FILE, applying changes to its files while it runs
  lube --build [--native [--fast]] [--small] FILE [-o OUT]
                        build FILE and its imports into a standalone executable; --native also
                        compiles its fns that compute only with Numbers and Bools to machine
                        code (needs a C compiler, and Lube's sources: LUBE_SRC); --fast lets
                        that code use 64-bit integers that wrap around and reorder sums;
                        --small makes it as small as it can be: only what of Lube and of the
                        program can run, compiled (needs a C compiler too)
  lube -v, --version    print the version
  lube -h, --help       show this help
[exit 0]
